# Audio, in any letter case, and Godot's import files beside it: every sound is
# generated with ElevenLabs, whose terms forbid making the output available as
# isolated audio files, and this repository is public (owner, 2026-11-14). The
# prompts and the tool that makes the audio are here (tools/sfx/README.md); the
# audio stays private. tools/check_sfx.mjs fails if Git tracks any.
*.[wW][aA][vV]
*.[wW][aA][vV].import
*.[oO][gG][gG]
*.[oO][gG][gG].import
*.[oO][gG][aA]
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[mM][pP]3.import
*.[fF][lL][aA][cC]
*.[oO][pP][uU][sS]
*.[mM]4[aA]
*.[aA][aA][cC]
*.[aA][iI][fF]
*.[aA][iI][fF][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][aA]
# The game's sound folder: everything tools/fetch-sfx writes there (the takes,
# their import files and manifest.json) but the note that explains it.
/game/resources/audio/sfx/*
!/game/resources/audio/sfx/README.md
